  "problem": "A native lethal hit expired the victim auras and closed its queued turn before trying resurrection. Trigger recorded the recipient but actually cast from the attacker at turn0. Mechanical723 and Damned724 author their effects at turn1, and the old Undead branch selected242 instead of724. Dead target filtering and the already-closed round prevented the native resurrection rows. Ordinary death dispatched twice; failed Kill could mark a live pet dead. Undead242 expiry killed both its owner and the opposing front pet.",
  "repair": "Attempt the two native racial reactions on the actual victim before committing final death. Consume the matching passive once, use real723/724turn1 and native trigger event10, and admit only a bounded existing dead caster for this internal context. Allow that caster through native corpse filtering; preserve the ordinary final-death aura cleanup. Use native percentage health with64bit intermediate/minimum living health and success checks. Clamp real pet health to0..max. Failed/already-dead kills return without side effects; final death dispatch occurs once.242terminal effect addresses only its actual owner and cannot kill the opponent. Immediate resurrection retains the queued native action and current round.",
  "native_data": "Matching26972 stores plus readonlyHotfix: initialization291 sets species family passives48/50;723turn1121 orders1/2/3 remove822,resurrect20percent,add244;724turn1122 removes822,resurrect1percent,add242duration1. Aura242 adds unkillable68 and damage-dealt23=-25 and has actual expiry5/property135. No invented resurrection health or timer.",
